    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0844" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7794</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Vopicka</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-23T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 23, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. Referring to Department’s 91, November 28,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d739-f1"/>
                    please reiterate assurances conveyed by the President to the King of Roumania.
                    Full text of President’s address to Congress was repeated to you by radio from
                    Saloniki. This Government has no knowledge of any understanding between Roumania
                    and her other allies in regard to peace terms,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d739-f2"/>
                    but is, however, committed to safeguard the integrity and freedom of smaller
                    nations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
